From: AD5X Open OS
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: ingenic: no rotator line padding on the AD5X

The rotator support pads every framebuffer line to the next 512-byte
multiple (3584 bytes for 800 px at 32 bpp). The AD5X never rotates, and
userspace (LVGL) derives bits per pixel from the stride, so the padded
stride left HelixScreen without a draw buffer.

diff --git a/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/x2600_rotate.h b/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/x2600_rotate.h
index cde97a9b5..bd84767aa 100644
--- a/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/x2600_rotate.h
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/video/fbdev/ingenic/fb_stage_wip/x2600_rotate.h
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@ static inline int rotator_aligned_size(int sz)
 {
 	//#define CEIL_ALIGN(size,aligned)  ((size + aligned - 1) / aligned * aligned)
 #define CEIL_ALIGN(size,aligned)  (((size) / aligned + 1) * aligned)
-#ifdef CONFIG_ROT_INGENIC
+#if 0	/* AD5X: never rotates; userspace derives bpp from the stride */
 	return CEIL_ALIGN(sz, 512);
 #else
 	return sz;
